<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Quado: third-party licenses</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #ffffff; color: #1d1d1f; }
  main { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 48px; }
  a { color: #1b5fc1; }
  ul.crates { columns: 2; padding-left: 20px; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f5f5f7; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13px; }
  h3 { margin-top: 32px; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { background: #1c1c1e; color: #f5f5f7; }
    a { color: #7fb0ff; }
    pre { background: #2a2a2d; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Quado: third-party licenses</h1>
<p>quado.exe includes the Rust crates listed below. Each section gives a license, the crates that use it and the license text. Quado itself is under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (LICENSE.txt). The licenses of the fonts Inter and IBM Plex are in the licenses folder of the zip file.</p>

<h2>Licenses</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>License texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
  {{#if first_of_kind}}<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>{{/if}}
  <p>Used by:</p>
  <ul class="crates">
  {{#each used_by}}
    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
  {{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</main>
</body>
</html>
